+## D1.8 F1 correction — complete shared lock protocol and consumer dispositions
+
+This section replaces r1's incomplete inherited-account/terminal-owner disposition. Keep synchronous notice composition/provable outbox insertion for ordinary pinned/unflagged Business, protected action, token and final-response decisions. Do not weaken those inherited assertions by switching them all to deferred notice mode.
+
+Introduce one bounded ReviewerAccountHints collection phase, with typed source identities/fingerprints and principal→account mappings, before any company/member/principal/run/source/event lock. It merges run actor, authenticated requester, command actor/reviewer where applicable, frozen final-response policy reviewers, root token-policy reviewers, and the current execution's Business/approval reviewers. Parse only the actual typed reviewer fields, never arbitrary UUIDs in JSON. Business inputs not frozen yet are previewed through the existing read-only activation resolution (activation.rs127–171) from immutable saved binding/context/prior outputs, without activating, consuming budget, taking locks, or writing anything; extract/reuse that resolver, do not implement a second evaluator. Current role reviewers are hinted through the frozen admission manifest for ordinary parking, and through live context for opt-in following. Action approval inputs already reside in frozen_inputs. At most16 reviewers per source and the fixed five source categories bound this hint set (plus actor/requester/command actor); enforce the aggregate bound before allocating/locking. Missing/unusable hints are a typed authorization/validation outcome, never an empty silently successful set.
+
+Lock the UNION of discovered account IDs once, sorted/deduplicated SHARE, before company serialization. Do not call the old final-policy-only prelocker first and then acquire extra users after it already locked company. After company NO KEY UPDATE, re-read all source identities/selector inputs, policies and mappings and compare exactly with the hint fingerprint. A changed set causes transaction rollback and a bounded retry/defer at its owning queue/command; never acquire a newly discovered user late. The actual locked activation/current authority remains decisive. eligible_reviewer_row and workflow_decision_person_snapshot may retain their current account SHARE checks only because the complete applicable users are already locked. User preferences are locked after that user's SHARE lock; account teardown cannot pass that first lock. Preserve current payload-clearance, verified-email/channel visibility, owner/admin protected-action/token/final-response restrictions, opt-out truth and atomic notice composition/insertion.
+
+The complete prelock integration belongs at each transaction owner, before the first company/run row:
+
+| Producer/consumer | Required disposition |
+| --- | --- |
+| Business WorkflowDecisions::park_decision, including unflagged and pinned | discover immutable/current execution reviewers without activating, merge all categories, ordered prelock, company, then waits/run/execution/park; exact hint revalidation before insertion |
+| Protected action dispatch/approval park, including model-tool actions | action_authority::prelock_accounts_on becomes the merged collector; all dispatch transaction entries call it before company/run/action locks, not inside late approvers |
+| Token reserve and settle paths that can park token allowance | merge token reviewers into the same account union BEFORE their company/root/run/fence lock; replace token_budget::prelock_reviewers' late independent authority discovery with verification of this prelocked exact set; preserve token authority and root ownership |
