+## D1.9 F2 correction — no recursive escalation from notification handling
+
+An escalation-generated admission carries an immutable, authenticated notification-origin fact: company/case/recipient-notice identity, canonical message/intent, and the admitted handling root. The notification commit writes message+intent+origin fact in the SAME fenced transaction. This is not a client/wire header or a caller-provided origin enum. Composite relationships bind the fact to the real case recipient/event/message/intent; updates and forged cross-source attachments fail. Admission copies it to an immutable run-origin relation; children and reruns retain that origin. All application-generated messages/effects from such runs carry the same durable internal causality through canonical message provenance and authenticated internal relay ingestion, so a new root or cross-desk relay cannot wash it away. Ordinary messages authored by a newly authenticated person are new user work and do not inherit it merely by sharing a thread. External headers cannot mint, remove or impersonate this provenance.
+
+A notification-origin root and all its descendants are INELIGIBLE to create another automatic escalation case, regardless of binding policy, reason, fresh run/source ID or repeated refusal. When an actual notice handling admission refuses or its run fails without an authored handler, record a bounded typed handling_failure fact against the ORIGINAL recipient/case, not a new case. A same-company downstream root inherits this rule. Cross-company internally relayed effects preserve a server-authenticated suppression marker bound to the real originating delivery provenance; they cannot create an automatic escalation chain in the destination, and cannot read or mutate the source case without its tenant relationship. The original recipient's actual own run outcome remains its settlement source. A human manually starting unrelated work is not silently suppressed.
+
+Once every recipient of a hop is provably undeliverable/failed/retired, expedite that case's already-unique next control event (or owner attention when no allowed hop remains). If at least one is still capable, retain the original acknowledgement deadline. A successfully completed handling workflow does not forge acknowledgement: the explicit authenticated decision command is still required. A successfully handled authored error route does not report unhandled failure. Terminal handling failure is visible in the original escalation history and, once ladder exhausted, owner waiting. Idempotent terminal fact keys avoid repeated wakeups. No new automatic case is emitted from those failure facts. Two automatic hops×at most16 recipients, plus at most32 explicit manual assignments, bound notification-created root admissions per case at64; existing per-run/dependency/relay budgets bound subsequent effects. Manual assignment is an explicit authenticated action, not an automatic way around the cap.
+
+Production tests drive actual worker→canonical agent notice→message admission→real refusal/failure for self-target and two-agent cross-desk cycles, including the downstream generated-message path, child and rerun inheritance. Assert the exact finite case/hop/notice/root counts, original-case handling_failure/owner-attention facts, no new recursive case/provider loop and replay idempotency. A fake origin boolean or a direct SQL terminal event is not the required evidence. A normal user message still creates its ordinary escalation. Test forged/missing/wrong-tenant origin relationships and internal-versus-untrusted-wire provenance.
+
+## D1.10 F3 correction — neutral notification-role truth table
+
+Escalation uses a dedicated neutral NotificationRecipients resolver, NOT model Agent or decision People mode. Find the nearest populated role in the frozen originating department's CURRENT bounded ancestry. A local populated role shadows the ancestor even if its members later prove ineligible; do not silently filter it to empty and choose another ancestor. Snapshot the complete selected local principal set (limit16); then assess each principal's current eligible delivery/action route independently. No arbitrary first holder or single-agent assumption.
+
+| Nearest set | Hop recipient facts/notices | Advance and reason |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| No role holder in ancestry | hop with explicit empty set, no recipient | immediate allowed hop2, otherwise owner; no_holder |
+| 1..16 eligible people | every person, deduplicated, ordinary notices | wait for ack deadline unless all become undeliverable |
+| 1..16 eligible agents | every agent (multiple supported), each current default desk | same; no model-mode wrong-kind/multiple-agent refusal |
+| Mixed people+agents, total1..16 | every eligible principal through its own adapter, immutable fact also records ineligible members | same; first valid acknowledgement settles the administrative decision for the hop |
+| Populated but all ineligible, retired, inaccessible or missing/disabled route | complete bounded set with per-recipient typed failure facts, no claimed-success notice | immediate next allowed hop/owner; no_eligible_recipient plus per-recipient detail |
+| Some ineligible but at least one eligible | preserve failures, notify ALL remaining eligible principals | wait for acknowledgement; do not advance solely because one route failed |
+| More than16 holders in nearest populated department | explicit recipient_limit refusal on hop; no subset delivered and no arbitrary truncation | immediate next allowed hop/owner; recipient_limit |
+
+Person eligibility requires current person/member identity, subject visibility/payload clearance for acting, and existing preference rules for email (opt-out still permits in-app and acknowledgement). Agent eligibility requires current agent identity, active enabled default desk/binding and actual command/run_as authority; a role never grants extra access or an administrative operation. Neutral role resolution itself accepts both kinds; whether an agent can act is an explicit per-recipient eligibility result, not a kind rejection. Wrong/unknown/system/external kinds are ineligible, never coerced to an account. Persist the original trigger reason separately from delivery/advance disposition, so a missing route does not overwrite the run failure cause. Hop2 applies the same neutral semantics to parent lead (normally single by department invariant). The over-bound result records a bounded count/refusal without retaining an unbounded list.
+
+Test person-only, multiple-agent-only, heterogeneous, local-ineligible shadowing ancestor, empty, exactly16 and17 via actual role writers and notification worker/projector/ladder. Assert every expected principal/message/notification and no subset/extra ancestor notice, exact failure/advance reason and current authority. Existing model Agent and decision People truth tables are unchanged.
